// this: its named arguments are inlined into it). Its names are words (`(made class: …)` is a group), its first value not
// a definition (`(class: P (x) => { … })` is a group). (Its brackets written as text, so it is not read as a closure.)
{`(`}{name}:{ }{value}, {{rest}}{`)`} =>
  (goto record) unless ("{name}" contains " ") || ("{value}" contains " => ")
  goto .
  record\
  {
    {name}: {value}
    {rest}
  }
{`(`}{name}:{ }{value}{`)`} =>
  (goto record) unless ("{name}" contains " ") || ("{value}" contains " => ")
  goto .
  record\
  {
    {name}: {value}
  }

// Ray: a chain of vertices, each holding a value (`head` the first vertex, `tail` the last; a vertex's `next`, `previous`).
// Called on a Ray (`r.append(1)`), `.` in a method is that Ray.
// (the list the language reads (`[…]`, `a, b`) is `Listing`, made at the end, in Iterable: what the library adds to
// Iterable is its too, below its own)
// (anything but a Ray read on: not a listing)
listing := false

// (A list, `a, b`: see `,` below, the loosest.)

